"""Batch03 bounded physical review from inspected raw windows; root accepts separately."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv, json
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
R=B.parent
CASES={
'Q021':('REFUTED','S62 has a broad, shallow trough with asymmetric adjacent variability. The S94 BTJD 3875 trough is the shared long S94 gap/step waveform present in Q024, Q026 and Q030; its local fit reaches a width bound. The two selected flags therefore do not show same-kind source-specific recurrence.','An isolated real dip elsewhere is not excluded. The S62 trough alone cannot establish an orbit.','Find a complete, target-centered dip in an independent sector.'),
'Q022':('REFUTED','The many S9/S10/S36/S37 and S63/S90/S99/S100 selected minima sit within continuous, roughly sinusoidal, changing-amplitude oscillations. Neighboring crests/troughs have the same shape, and several local trapezoids are singular or depth-bound. These are repeating brightness variations, but not discrete eclipse cores at the selected windows.','The selected eclipse interpretation is refuted by the oscillatory context; the underlying variability is physically interesting and may be stellar pulsation or rotation.','Characterize the oscillation spectrum if desired; require an isolated eclipse core for an EB claim.'),
'Q023':('PLAUSIBLE','The S18 BTJD 1805.8, S58 2906.2 and S85 3624.0 selected troughs occur amid large, irregular, multi-day raw variability. S18 is an asymmetric complex low with recovery and adjacent excursions; S58 and S85 are smaller undulations of similar scale to their surrounding variations. No stable same-kind eclipse morphology or measured cycle count is established.','Individual dips might contain real eclipses, so the binary interpretation remains insecure rather than positively refuted. The selection Gaia period is not an event-derived clock.','Obtain an isolated full repeated dip with stable shape and test integer-cycle aliases.'),
'Q024':('REFUTED','The S94 BTJD 3874.95 flag is the same shared broad gap/step waveform seen in Q021/Q026/Q030. The much larger S95 BTJD 3895.83 local fit extrapolates across a long missing interval, is singular and boundary-limited, and has only a gap-edge recovery; its nominal 141-ppt depth is not a measured eclipse. The other S95 flag tracks a sector-scale rise.','The selected signals do not establish source-specific eclipses. The large gap-edge fit is unusable as an eclipse depth.','Look for a fully observed dip with both local baselines and valid source pixels.'),
'Q025':('PLAUSIBLE','S5 BTJD 1454.341 and S32 BTJD 2178.169 show similar short, approximately 3-ppt raw dips, also present in KSPSAP on the same photons. Independent TESSCut difference loss peaks within about 0.2 pixel of the Gaia target in both sectors, supporting target attribution at TESS resolution. The S5 egress is followed by a 0.146-d cadence gap, but the dip and immediate egress are observed; S32 is complete. Their 723.828-d separation allows many integer cycle counts. A bounded check of counts 10-20 (36.19-72.38 d) finds no additional predicted event inside either cached sector to discriminate them. Fourteen cycles give 51.7020 d, only conditionally close to the Gaia 51.62784-d spectroscopic period; source-specific conjunction timing remains untested.','Exact Gaia identity is already a published EB alert (Tarrants and Mendes Table 2) and appears in Chopard v1.2.0; novelty is known. This bounded two-occasion review does not by itself validate the selected dips as that published eclipse clock. Unresolved close neighbors remain possible.','Recover the published ephemeris and a third target-localized event; check Gaia conjunction geometry and cycle aliases.'),
'Q026':('REFUTED','The S94 BTJD 3874.95 flag repeats the common gap-linked waveform of Q021/Q024/Q030. The S94 3869.6 deep fit is across a broad interval with missing data and singular boundary-limited parameters. S101 4107.9 is a baseline step/trend with a width-bound fit, not the same eclipse shape.','Selected flags lack a reproducible isolated core. The fitted deep event and selected depths are not adopted.','Require a full, source-specific dip with both baselines.'),
'Q027':('PLAUSIBLE','S10 BTJD 1588.414 and S100 4075.502 contain narrow, fully sampled raw dips of roughly 4-5 ppt, with the S10 feature retained in KSPSAP. Independent TESSCut difference images place the loss at the target position in both sectors. S101 BTJD 4119.39 contains a dip-like excursion amid dense quality gaps and an abrupt baseline change; its local center is not precise enough to prove another same-kind occasion. Explicit cycle counts 50-64 were projected into all cached sectors: n=56 and 58 predict complete S64 cores at BTJD 3054.020 and 3046.362, with local detrended depths -0.17 and -0.06 ppt rather than a 4-ppt dip. These are useful nulls for those two aliases. Several other counts lack discriminating coverage, and n=57 (43.6331 d) remains conditional; the Gaia period is not an adopted photometric clock.','Two clean target-position occasions and a compromised third leave unresolved subpixel neighbors, remaining integer aliases and orbital conjunction geometry.','Obtain a third complete target-localized dip or further sensitive alias nulls, then test Gaia conjunction geometry.'),
'Q028':('REFUTED','S94 BTJD 3875.09 is the same broad shared S94 gap/step feature as Q021/Q024/Q026/Q030. S95 3896.1 and S102 4133.7/4146.9 are steps or long baseline trends with width-bound local fits; S103 4165 is dominated by a gap-edge recovery and singular boundary fit. These do not reproduce a discrete same-kind eclipse.','The selected-window verdict leaves unrelated variability unclassified. No fitted period or depth is adopted.','Find an isolated full dip with consistent morphology and target-centered pixels.'),
'Q029':('REFUTED','There are many real short raw dips in S4, S5 and S31. Twelve selected local centers give a conditional 1.9634497-d dip clock with 0.00615-d RMS; the ±1 long-baseline cycle aliases smear the narrow cores. Full-cycle extraction finds 22 complete predicted cores. However, independent TESSCut difference images in all three sectors localize the loss at nearby Gaia DR3 4883892013333719680 (G=12.8691), several pixels from the selected Gaia DR3 4883891772815552000. Thus the repeated aperture dips are real but do not belong to the selected Gaia SB1 source, whose spectroscopic period is also incompatible at 46.08764 d.','The selected target-associated EB interpretation is refuted by positive spatial attribution to a different star. The neighbor may itself be an EB: odd/even depth differences of about 0.2-0.3 ppt recur in all three sectors, with exploratory sector-stratified permutation p≈0.016. A 1P transiting body remains possible, and aperture dilution limits companion sizing. The selected TIC radius is 2.294 solar radii, but it does not apply to the eclipsed neighbor.','Analyze source-resolved neighbor photometry to distinguish 1.96345-d transits from 3.9269-d alternating eclipses; review the selected Gaia SB1 separately for its own orbital eclipses.'),
'Q030':('REFUTED','S94 BTJD 3875.11 and S104 4197.33 are broad gap-linked shared waveforms, matching Q021/Q024/Q026 in S94 and earlier reviewed common-mode examples in S104. The S94 3869.45 fit extrapolates over a long missing interval and is singular/boundary-limited. No isolated source-specific repeated eclipse core emerges from these flags.','This refutes the selected bulk flags as binary evidence, not every possible variability signal from the star.','Seek a complete target-localized raw dip in a separate observing occasion.'),
}
fields=['sample_id','tic','sample_stratum','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status','period_days','period_error_days','primary_epoch_btjd','depth_ppt','limitations','next_check','report']
rows=[]
for q in csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(encoding='utf8',newline='')):
    sid=q['sample_id'];tic=q['tic'];verdict,finding,limits,next_check=CASES[sid]
    d=json.loads((B/tic/'lead-measurements.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
    status='KNOWN' if sid=='Q025' else 'UNKNOWN'
    selected=', '.join(f"S{x['sector']} {x['screen_center_btjd']:.3f}" for x in d['screen_flagged_dips'])
    if len(selected)>450:selected=selected[:447]+'...'
    report=(B/tic/'REPORT.md').resolve()
    lines=[f'# {sid} / TIC {tic}','',f'**Physical verdict:** {verdict}. **Novelty:** {status}.','',
           '## Raw result','',finding,'',f'Selected detector windows (BTJD predictions, not adopted event centers): {selected}. Full measured local windows, fits, actual sector coverage and SHA-256 source receipts are in `lead-measurements.json`; raw plots in `lead-event-panels.png`. Actual core/wing endpoints and gaps are in `lead-window-checks.json`. Same-photon KSPSAP comparison, where available, is in `lead-alternative.json` and its plot.','',
           '## Orbit, source and limits','',f'Frozen Gaia DR3 source {q["gaia_dr3"]} has spectroscopic period {float(q["gaia_period_days"]):.6f} d. This is a selection prior, not a measured eclipse period or a source-specific conjunction match.','',limits,'']
    if sid=='Q025':lines+=['Catalogue receipts: `../../shared-catalogues/TARGET-STATUS.csv`, `../../shared-catalogues/tarrants-mendes-overlaps.json` and `../../shared-catalogues/chopard-overlaps.json`. Independent difference images/WCS: `../helper-q025-difference.json` and associated PNG; TESSCut source ZIP hashes are recorded there. Conditional cycle calculations and cached-sector availability: `lead-alias-checks.json`. Publication identity and physical interpretation of these two particular dips are separate claims.','']
    elif sid=='Q027':lines+=['Independent difference images/WCS for S10 and S100: `../helper-q027-difference.json` and associated PNG; TESSCut source ZIP hashes are recorded there. Conditional cycle counts, actual cadence coverage and bounded S64 nulls: `lead-alias-checks.json` and `lead-alias-nulls.png`.','']
    elif sid=='Q029':lines+=['Conditional timing and adjacent-cycle alias residuals: `lead-timing.json`; phase plot: `lead-phase.png`; every covered predicted event and odd/even depths: `lead-all-cycles.json`. Independent source-resolved WCS and difference-flux evidence: `../helper-q029-difference.json`, associated PNG, `../helper-q029-apertures.json` and helper audit. Neighbor-centered apertures have roughly 80-130-ppt dips, whereas target-centered apertures show no corresponding loss at the 0.1-ppt scale. The TIC radius metadata and hash are in `lead-timing.json`; that radius concerns the selected target, not the contaminating neighbor. The photometric dip clock is intentionally not placed in the orbital-period field.','']
    else:lines+=['Catalogue status is UNKNOWN: fresh VSX, ASAS-SN and Kostov gates failed in the queue-wide audit; failure is not a nonmatch.','']
    lines+=['This is a bounded verdict on the selected bulk lead, not a global statement that the star has no binary or transit signal. A same-photon reduction is a processing comparison, not a new observing occasion.','', '## Next check','',next_check,'']
    report.write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf8')
    rows.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,sample_stratum=q['sample_stratum'],physical_verdict=verdict,full_review_completion='COMPLETE',novelty_status=status,period_days='',period_error_days='',primary_epoch_btjd='',depth_ppt='',limitations=limits,next_check=next_check,report=str(report)))
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',encoding='utf8',newline='') as f:
    w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
print([(x['sample_id'],x['physical_verdict']) for x in rows])
